Instead of the boring "You feel that [godname] is angry" could we have some
more options? In the old version of Amiga Hack (1.0.3d I think, by the Software
Distillery) when you prayed you sometimes got a message like
 
"Elbereth Gilthoniel and associates. Please hold the line." -more-
"Mr. Elbereth is in a meeting. Please leave a message" -more-

Then you enter some text.
 
I'm not sure what the text did, but it was more fun than just having an angry
god all the time. You could also have a delay while you're holding the 
line, so that if monsters were close and you prayed and got the above then
you would be at their mercy until the gods took you off hold. I think it's
a nice alternative to a -1 luck and an angry message every time you pray too
soon. The paralysis while on hold could be easily as deadly as a lightning
bolt from the heavens if you're next to a Minotaur, but then again it could
mean nothing to you if you were all alone. Perhaps some elvish songs or
something to read while on hold? What do the rest of you think?

